WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
A baby reaches for a bright, squeaky toy.

2
00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:06.490
Drop a blanket over it, and
the baby just looks away.

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.140
As far as they're
concerned, it's vanished.

4
00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.560
A year later: same toy, same blanket.

5
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.480
This time they yank the
blanket straight off.

6
00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:16.660
Better eyesight?

7
00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.770
Did someone show them where to look?

8
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.190
Why can the older child find it?

9
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.570
In this mission, you'll see
how children build schemas:

10
00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.930
mental frameworks of knowledge,
built from experience.

11
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:32.480
And you'll climb Piaget's four stages,
which every child goes through in the same

12
00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:33.390
order.

13
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.480
The first is the sensorimotor stage,
learning through senses and movement.

14
00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:42.840
Your mission: work out why the
older child can find the hidden toy.
